<<16 Prompt>> Give me an algebra exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on evaluating expressions. It should have multiple steps. There should be marks/points assigned to the question. It should be a with Answer. <<Prompt>>
<<16 Generation>> Evaluate the following expressions:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( 3n + 5 \) when \( n = 6 \) (2 marks)
\item \( 10 - 4m \) when \( m = 7 \) (2 marks)
\item \( 12 - 2p \) when \( p = 5 \) (2 marks)
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( 3n + 5 = 3(6) + 5 = 18 + 5 = 23 \)
\item \( 10 - 4m = 10 - 4(7) = 10 - 28 = -18 \)
\item \( 12 - 2p = 12 - 2(5) = 12 - 10 = 2 \)
\end{enumerate} <<Generation>>
