<<833 Prompt>> Give me a combination of a challenge exercise, a long answer exercise, and a question for a 4th grade student learning history. <<Prompt>>
<<833 Generation>> Why did Ancient Egyptian merchants travel to other countries to trade? What did they hope to bring back to Ancient Egypt? Why did other countries want to trade with Ancient Egypt? What did they have to offer the Egyptians? Write a paragraph to answer these questions. Try to imagine what it would be like to travel to another country to trade goods. What challenges would you face? What would you see? What would you eat? How would you travel? How long would it take? How would you carry the goods? How would you keep them safe? Write a paragraph to describe a journey you would make to trade goods in Ancient Egyptian times. Choose a country to travel to and describe the journey, what you see and the goods you bring back. Use your imagination to help you write this description. Think about:  
\begin{itemize}
\item how you feel as you set off on your journey
\item the different landscapes you see on the way
\item the people you meet on the way  
\item how you will travel and how you will carry the goods  
\item how long the journey takes  
\item what the goods are and why they are wanted in Ancient Egypt  
\item how you will keep the goods safe.  
\end{itemize}  
Write a final paragraph to describe how trade helped the Egyptian civilisation to develop. Explain how trade helped the different classes within the civilisation. Think about:  
\begin{itemize}
\item how the goods helped the farmers  
\item how the goods helped the artisans  
\item how the goods helped the scribes  
\item how the goods helped the nobles  
\item how the goods helped the pharaoh.  
\end{itemize}  
Explain how trade helped the civilisation as a whole. Think about:  
\begin{itemize}
\item how the goods helped the army  
\item how the goods helped the size of the population  
\item how the goods helped the power of the pharaoh  
\item how the goods helped the towns and cities to develop.  
\end{itemize}  
Finally, think about how trade helped the civilisation to become more complex. Think about:  
\begin{itemize}
\item the different jobs people had  
\item the different amounts of money people had  
\item the different sizes of the houses people lived in  
\item the different amounts of food people had.  
\end{itemize}  
Think about how the goods helped to make these differences between people. How did the goods help some people to have more money, better houses and more food? How did the goods help other people to have less money, worse houses and less food? How did this help the civilisation to become more complex? Explain your ideas in your final paragraph. <<Generation>>
